Here is the commit message:
fixed a bug

Here is the root cause:
The `GridView` instance in `MainActivityFragment` was never explicitly bound to its `imageAdapter` via `setAdapter()` after being retrieved through `findViewById()`. Although `updateUI()` was called to presumably populate or update `imageAdapter`'s data, without calling `gridview.setAdapter(imageAdapter)`, the `GridView` had no adapter attached to render its items. This means the view had no data source to pull from, resulting in an empty or non-functional grid (movie posters not displaying), since Android's `GridView`/`AdapterView` requires an explicit `setAdapter()` call to link the view with its data-backing adapter — simply updating the adapter's internal data without binding it to the view has no visual effect.

Here is the patch:

     @Override
     public View onCreateView(LayoutInflater inflater, ViewGroup container,
                              Bundle savedInstanceState) {
         mainFragmentView = inflater.inflate(R.layout.fragment_main, container, false);
         mRequestQueue = Volley.newRequestQueue(getContext());

         // setup image adapter
         imageAdapter = new ImageAdapter(getContext());

         updateUI();
         gridview = (GridView) mainFragmentView.findViewById(R.id.gridView);
+        gridview.setAdapter(imageAdapter);

         gridview.setOnItemClickListener(new AdapterView.OnItemClickListener() {
             @Override
             public void onItemClick(AdapterView<?> adapterView, View view, int position, long id) {
                 Intent intent = new Intent(getContext(), DetailActivity.class).putExtra(Intent.EXTRA_TEXT, position + "");
                 startActivity(intent);
             }
         });

         return mainFragmentView;
     }



